#: ../../source/incoming/controller_attributes.rst:39
msgid ""
"The ``Filters`` attribute allows you to specify one or more filters to be"
" applied to a controller class or method. You can specify filters to run "
"before or after the controller action, and you can also provide "
"parameters to the filters. Here's an example of how to use the "
"``Filters`` attribute:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/controller_attributes.rst:45
msgid ""
"When filters are applied both by an attribute and in the filter "
"configuration file, they will both be applied, but that could lead to "
"unexpected results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/incoming/controller_attributes.rst:49
msgid ""
"Please remember that every parameter applied to the filter will be "
"converted to a string. This behavior affects only filters."
msgstr ""

